Solving cos(60 + x) + 2 * sin(30 + x) = 0 for x

Expanding and collecting terms gives

-1 * sin(x) * (sin(60) + -2 * cos(30)) + (3/2) * cos(x) = 0

tan(x) = - (cos(30) * 2 + sin(60) * -1) / (3/2) 

	Letting n1 denote an arbitrary integer
    x = arctan((2/3) * (1 * sin(60) + -2 * cos(30))) + 180 * n1
